          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.138,
            0.828,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the dimensions of the prayer hall discussed in Section 4.1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.164,
            0.901,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Section 4.1, we found that if the breadth of the hall is x m, then x satisfies the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2}+x-300=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Applying the factorisation method, we write this equation as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.227,
            0.518,
            0.246
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "2x^{2}-24x+25x-300=0"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.252,
            0.518,
            0.272
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "2x\\left (x-12  \\right ) +25\\left (x-12  \\right ) =0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.279,
            0.139,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.278,
            0.518,
            0.297
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "(x - 12)(2x + 25) = 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.304,
            0.9,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the roots of the given equation are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 12   or   x = -12.5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Since x is the breadth of the hall, it cannot be negative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.347,
            0.71,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the breadth of the hall is 12 m. Its length = 2x + 1 = 25 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.387,
            0.586,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISE 4.2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.417,
            0.749,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the roots of the following quadratic equations by factorisation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.447,
            0.342,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x^{2}-3x-10=0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.447,
            0.702,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} + x - 6 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.476,
            0.401,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt{2} x^{2} + 7x + 5\\sqrt{2} = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.537,
            0.469,
            0.711,
            0.506
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "2x^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{8}=0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.506,
            0.372,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "100x^{2}-20x+1=0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.529,
            0.497,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Solve the problems given in Example 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.552,
            0.633,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find two numbers whose sum is 27 and product is 182."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.573,
            0.759,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find two consecutive positive integers, sum of whose squares is 365."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.595,
            0.901,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The altitude of a right triangle is 7 cm less than its base. If the hypotenuse is 13 cm, find the other two sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.635,
            0.902,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A cottage industry produces a certain number of pottery articles in a day. It was observed on a particular day that the cost of production of each article (in rupees) was 3 more than twice the number of articles produced on that day. If the total cost of production on that day was ` 90, find the number of articles produced and the cost of each article."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.719,
            0.325,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.4 Nature of Roots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.745,
            0.516,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2} + bx + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are given by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.773,
            0.545,
            0.821
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_24.jpg",
          "content": "x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.823,
            0.902,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b ^ { 2 }   -   4 a c   >   0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we get two distinct real roots "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- { \\frac { b } { 2 a } } + { \\frac { \\sqrt { b ^ { 2 } - 4 a c } } { 2 a } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-   { \\frac { b } { 2 a } } - { \\frac { \\sqrt { b ^ { 2 } - 4 a c } } { 2 a } } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 26,
